[{"text": "The assembly will hear an address by his", "start": 2.48, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "excellency Everest", "start": 5.279, "duration": 6.721}, {"text": "India Shimi, President of the Republic", "start": 8.24, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "of Burundi.", "start": 12.0, "duration": 3.24}, {"text": "I request protocol to escort his", "start": 17.68, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "excellency and invite him to address the", "start": 20.08, "duration": 5.88}, {"text": "assembly.", "start": 22.96, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "in the name of God the all powerful most", "start": 40.64, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "merciful", "start": 44.48, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "distinguished president of the general", "start": 46.239, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "assembly Mr. Secretary General,", "start": 48.399, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "excellencies,", "start": 50.64, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "heads of state and government, ladies", "start": 53.52, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "and gentlemen,", "start": 55.52, "duration": 6.719}, {"text": "as President of the Republic of Burundi", "start": 57.68, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "and the current chairperson of the", "start": 62.239, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "African Union,", "start": 64.08, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "allow me", "start": 66.08, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "to first on behalf of the people of", "start": 68.159, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "Burundi and of Africa", "start": 70.56, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "and congratulate his excellency Dr.", "start": 73.36, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "Khalilur", "start": 76.56, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "Rahman,", "start": 78.159, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "president of the General Assembly of the", "start": 80.4, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "United Nations on his election and wish", "start": 83.52, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "him every success in the fulfillment of", "start": 86.0, "duration": 6.28}, {"text": "his mandate.", "start": 89.119, "duration": 3.161}, {"text": "I would like to take this opportunity to", "start": 92.56, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "extend my warmest congratulations and", "start": 95.439, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "express my deepest gratitude to his", "start": 98.079, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "excellency Mr. Antonio Gutierrez,", "start": 101.04, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "Secretary General of the United Nations,", "start": 104.479, "duration": 7.68}, {"text": "for the unwavering commitment and", "start": 109.04, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "dedication he has demonstrated", "start": 112.159, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "throughout his tenure in the service of", "start": 114.479, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "peace, security,", "start": 117.68, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "and sustainable development around the", "start": 120.32, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "world. His good offices", "start": 122.64, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "exercised with wisdom, humility, and", "start": 126.479, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "determination", "start": 129.28, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "have helped bridge", "start": 131.039, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "the widest divergences of opinion and", "start": 133.84, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "provided invaluable support to nations,", "start": 137.36, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "particularly those in the global south,", "start": 140.319, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "in their quest for stability and", "start": 142.72, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "prosperity.", "start": 145.36, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "Burundi,", "start": 147.2, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "which has always", "start": 148.72, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "been able to count on the United Nations", "start": 151.12, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "generous support, wishes to commend his", "start": 153.36, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "leadership", "start": 156.08, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "and his unwavering commitment to the", "start": 158.319, "duration": 7.081}, {"text": "principles of multilateralism.", "start": 160.8, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "As he prepares to turn this important", "start": 166.239, "duration": 7.201}, {"text": "page of his life,", "start": 170.48, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "I wish him on my own behalf and on", "start": 173.44, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "behalf of the entire Burundian people", "start": 175.92, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "every success in his new endeavors", "start": 178.239, "duration": 7.441}, {"text": "as well as good health and", "start": 181.68, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "a future filled with serenity and", "start": 185.68, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "prosperity. Excellencies, ladies and", "start": 187.92, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "gentlemen,", "start": 190.959, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "the theme of this 81st session,", "start": 192.8, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "restoring trust,", "start": 197.12, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "managing transformation,", "start": 199.44, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "a united nation that delivers for all.", "start": 202.08, "duration": 9.439}, {"text": "Comes at a time when our world faces", "start": 207.44, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "multiple crises.", "start": 211.519, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "aggression against states,", "start": 213.76, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "internal armed conflicts fueled from", "start": 216.799, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "outside, and expansionist conflicts that", "start": 219.36, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "are breeding mistrust among states and", "start": 223.44, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "rendering the international community", "start": 227.36, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "unable to resolve these crises through", "start": 229.599, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "peaceful means.", "start": 232.239, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "In this context, a fundamental question", "start": 234.159, "duration": 7.841}, {"text": "arises. How can we restore trust in", "start": 237.519, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "multilateralism", "start": 242.0, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "and ensure that international", "start": 243.68, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "institutions", "start": 246.239, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "truly meet the expectations of all", "start": 247.76, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "peoples?", "start": 250.959, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "Our answer is clear.", "start": 252.799, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "We must strengthen multilateralism,", "start": 255.439, "duration": 7.121}, {"text": "reform global governance,", "start": 259.199, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "and place human dignity at the heart of", "start": 262.56, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "our collective action.", "start": 265.6, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "Excellency is", "start": 267.84, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "peace first. Peace is the source of all", "start": 270.72, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "good. Peace in our hearts. Peace in our", "start": 273.68, "duration": 7.76}, {"text": "societies. Peace in our countries. Let", "start": 277.84, "duration": 7.6}, {"text": "us begin by restoring peace within our", "start": 281.44, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "own community. Let us consolidate peace", "start": 285.44, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "in our respective countries. Let us", "start": 287.12, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "rebuild trust among our peoples and", "start": 289.68, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "restore the image of humanity in our", "start": 293.199, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "midst.", "start": 296.32, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "This year when Burundi holds the", "start": 299.04, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "rotating chairmanship of the African", "start": 301.52, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Union, we are keenly aware of the", "start": 303.199, "duration": 7.041}, {"text": "responsibility that falls to us.", "start": 307.12, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "As the African Union champion for the", "start": 310.24, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "youth peace and security agenda,", "start": 313.28, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "I have this year once again convened a", "start": 316.16, "duration": 6.879}, {"text": "continental youth dialogue", "start": 320.08, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "coupled with the women peace and", "start": 323.039, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "security agenda.", "start": 324.72, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "During this dialogue, I sense the", "start": 326.88, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "enthusiasm of young people and women to", "start": 329.759, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "build a community with a shared future", "start": 333.36, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "in the spirit of Ubuntu.", "start": 335.36, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "In these young people, I sense the", "start": 337.919, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "desire to connect with one another", "start": 340.0, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "and to live together side by side. But", "start": 343.6, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "unfortunately,", "start": 346.4, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "there are still states that prevent", "start": 347.919, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "their citizens from living together with", "start": 350.08, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "other peoples as brothers and sisters.", "start": 352.8, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "They", "start": 354.8, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "cultivate and perpetuate xenophobia and", "start": 358.16, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "intolerance. They sow division by", "start": 363.039, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "failing to implement preventive and", "start": 366.16, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "corrective measures,", "start": 368.08, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "by highlighting disparities in", "start": 370.24, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "development, labeling some as rich and", "start": 372.639, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "others as poor, and thereby creating a", "start": 375.12, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "divide among peoples based on wealth and", "start": 378.88, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "material possessions.", "start": 382.4, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "And on that basis", "start": 384.479, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "they have come to regard themselves as", "start": 388.08, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "saints while reproaching others for", "start": 390.88, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "being inferior.", "start": 393.6, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "How then can we build trust among", "start": 396.16, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "nations without first", "start": 399.52, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "starting with building connection and", "start": 403.28, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "cohesion among our peoples.", "start": 404.8, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "We the leaders must rekindle the spirit", "start": 408.24, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "of Ubuntu within ourselves. The Ubuntu", "start": 411.36, "duration": 7.279}, {"text": "with which God created us. Indeed, God", "start": 414.639, "duration": 7.041}, {"text": "did not create a man who was selfish. He", "start": 418.639, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "created a man of Ubuntu. The Ubuntu that", "start": 421.68, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "I see in you and that you will find in", "start": 424.16, "duration": 7.759}, {"text": "me. Ubuntu is the common denominator", "start": 426.56, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "that must restore trust among all human", "start": 431.919, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "beings. Excellencies,", "start": 434.56, "duration": 7.359}, {"text": "as an African and a voice for Africa at", "start": 438.16, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "this time when I hold the rotating", "start": 441.919, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "chairmanship of the African Union,", "start": 443.52, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "I must also state the following. We are", "start": 446.56, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "here to", "start": 449.599, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "convey a conviction. Africa must be", "start": 452.0, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "listened to more. It must be better", "start": 454.56, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "represented and more closely involved in", "start": 456.56, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "the decisions that shape the future of", "start": 458.8, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "our planet.", "start": 461.12, "duration": 3.24}, {"text": "This is what must build trust between", "start": 464.96, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "Africa and other continents as well as", "start": 467.12, "duration": 7.199}, {"text": "with international institutions.", "start": 470.479, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "We no longer wish to see the Human", "start": 474.319, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "Rights Council become a forum for", "start": 476.319, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "oppressing countries that are", "start": 478.56, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "deliberately singled out because they", "start": 481.84, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "defend and fight for the interests of", "start": 483.84, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "their peoples.", "start": 485.44, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "We want to see this council working for", "start": 487.84, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "justice and equity for all states", "start": 491.68, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "without distinction.", "start": 494.56, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "International human rights law must", "start": 497.199, "duration": 6.801}, {"text": "apply without exception to all states of", "start": 500.16, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "the world both", "start": 504.0, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "in its corrective function as well as in", "start": 506.639, "duration": 6.721}, {"text": "its regulatory function.", "start": 510.16, "duration": 6.799}, {"text": "The Human Rights Council", "start": 513.36, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "cannot be instrumentalized by other", "start": 516.959, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "countries to the detriment of others", "start": 521.36, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "given that all member states of the", "start": 523.599, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "United Nations enjoy a status of", "start": 525.04, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "sovereign equality.", "start": 527.279, "duration": 3.401}, {"text": "Burundi wishes to reiterate once again", "start": 530.959, "duration": 8.161}, {"text": "its opposition to the imposition of a", "start": 534.64, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "special reporter in the situation of", "start": 539.12, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "human rights in Burundi which who was", "start": 540.72, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "appointed without any prior dialogue or", "start": 543.6, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "consultation.", "start": 546.08, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Burundi is a responsible country that", "start": 548.48, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "respects human rights.", "start": 551.68, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "It", "start": 554.88, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "has fought impunity for decades. It", "start": 556.64, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "upholds the rights and freedoms of all", "start": 559.12, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "and", "start": 562.16, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "ensures security as well as the", "start": 564.08, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "guarantee that crimes it has experienced", "start": 566.64, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "in the past will not be repeated. Mr.", "start": 568.72, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "President,", "start": 571.44, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Africa intends to be a full-fledged", "start": 574.32, "duration": 6.959}, {"text": "actor and not a mere observer", "start": 577.04, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "called upon to applaud decisions in", "start": 581.279, "duration": 7.68}, {"text": "whose preparation it played no part.", "start": 583.519, "duration": 8.561}, {"text": "Africa is not seeking any privileges. It", "start": 588.959, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "is demanding justice, equity, and", "start": 592.08, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "representation.", "start": 594.72, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "We therefore strongly reaffirm the need", "start": 598.56, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "for", "start": 602.399, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "reform of the United Nations Security", "start": 604.72, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "Council in order to allow for permanent", "start": 607.04, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "African representation and more", "start": 610.16, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "equitable participation", "start": 612.32, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "by the continent", "start": 614.64, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "in the international community's", "start": 616.72, "duration": 6.52}, {"text": "decision-making mechanisms.", "start": 619.519, "duration": 3.721}, {"text": "In this regard, Burundi believes that", "start": 623.44, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "discussions on reform", "start": 626.16, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "must also address the financial", "start": 629.12, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "viability of the United Nations system", "start": 631.04, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "by strengthening the predictability,", "start": 634.16, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "transparency,", "start": 636.24, "duration": 6.2}, {"text": "and sustainability of its financing.", "start": 638.0, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "It would not be coherent to entrust the", "start": 642.56, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "organization with ever greater", "start": 644.72, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "responsibilities", "start": 646.8, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "without guaranteeing it the resources", "start": 648.48, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "necessary for their implementation.", "start": 651.04, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "We therefore call on member states,", "start": 653.6, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "particularly the wealthiest, to", "start": 657.04, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "demonstrate responsibility and", "start": 659.2, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "solidarity", "start": 660.88, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "in order to preserve the organization's", "start": 662.56, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "financial stability. President,", "start": 665.68, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "excellencies, ladies and gentlemen,", "start": 668.88, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "as part of this process of reform,", "start": 672.0, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "strengthening and consolidation of our", "start": 675.36, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "organization, Burundi also wishes to", "start": 677.2, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "contribute to the debate on the", "start": 680.48, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "selection process for the next secretary", "start": 683.04, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "general of the United Nations.", "start": 684.8, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "In the current international context", "start": 687.36, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "marked by deep geopolitical divisions", "start": 689.12, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "and growing challenges to", "start": 692.8, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "multilateralism,", "start": 694.959, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "this process must be conducted in a spir", "start": 697.04, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "spirit of transparency, openness and", "start": 699.92, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "collective responsibility.", "start": 702.16, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "Bundi believes that this process must be", "start": 705.44, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "based above all on qualifications,", "start": 710.16, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "experience, integrity, independence of", "start": 712.88, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "judgment, diplomatic skill,", "start": 715.76, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "and the ability to bring together the", "start": 719.36, "duration": 6.76}, {"text": "positions of all member states.", "start": 722.0, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "We need a true bridgeuer,", "start": 726.16, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "a leader capable of engaging in dialogue", "start": 729.44, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "with all parties,", "start": 731.44, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "of bringing positions closer together", "start": 733.6, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "even when divergences appear", "start": 736.24, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "uncsurmountable, but also of showing", "start": 738.56, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "firmness, courage, and independence when", "start": 741.04, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "it comes to defending the principles of", "start": 744.56, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "the United Nations Charter and ensuring", "start": 747.04, "duration": 7.52}, {"text": "that the collective interest prevails.", "start": 751.2, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "Mr. President, excellencies, ladies and", "start": 754.56, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "gentlemen,", "start": 756.88, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "peace remains the primary condition for", "start": 758.88, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "development. The African Union is deeply", "start": 762.399, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "concerned by the persistence of", "start": 764.8, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "conflicts and crises", "start": 766.56, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "that continue to cause massive", "start": 769.12, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "population displacements,", "start": 771.76, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "destroy infrastructure,", "start": 773.839, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "and deprive millions of children of", "start": 777.12, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "their right to education", "start": 779.04, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "and to a better future.", "start": 781.279, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "We are paying particular attention to", "start": 785.04, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "the situation in the Great Lakes region,", "start": 787.2, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "in Sudan, Nahal, and Somalia,", "start": 790.399, "duration": 7.361}, {"text": "and in all regions facing violence and", "start": 794.48, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "instability.", "start": 797.76, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "We reaffirm our commitment to seeking", "start": 799.6, "duration": 7.6}, {"text": "African solutions to African problems", "start": 802.72, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "in accordance with international law and", "start": 807.2, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "the United Nations Charter.", "start": 809.44, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "We therefore called for a strengthened", "start": 812.0, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "partnership between the African Union", "start": 815.92, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "and the United Nations in the", "start": 818.16, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "prevention, mediation and peaceful", "start": 819.76, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "settlement of conflicts.", "start": 822.16, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "Bundi drawing on its experience will", "start": 825.839, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "continue to contribute to peace efforts", "start": 827.92, "duration": 7.08}, {"text": "on the continent.", "start": 831.6, "duration": 3.4}, {"text": "But we must go even further.", "start": 835.76, "duration": 6.879}, {"text": "As decided in Lwanda at the 21st", "start": 839.199, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "extraordinary session of the African", "start": 842.639, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "Union Assembly of Heads of State and", "start": 845.519, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Government, Africa must not only learn", "start": 846.959, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "to manage conflicts,", "start": 850.079, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "it must strengthen its capacity to", "start": 852.16, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "prevent them.", "start": 854.32, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "We also call on the international", "start": 856.399, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "community to lend greater support to", "start": 858.72, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "African peace and security mechanisms", "start": 861.6, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "in particular through predictable and", "start": 865.36, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "sustainable financing for African-led", "start": 867.68, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "peace operations.", "start": 870.56, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "Mr. President, excellencies, ladies and", "start": 872.88, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "gentlemen,", "start": 874.8, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "I would be remiss if I were to address", "start": 878.0, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "this August assembly without raising the", "start": 882.399, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "issue of water. The African Union has", "start": 885.44, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "designated 2026 as the year of", "start": 888.0, "duration": 7.839}, {"text": "assuring sustainable water availability", "start": 892.56, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "and safe sanitation systems to achieve", "start": 895.839, "duration": 5.881}, {"text": "the goals of agenda.", "start": 897.839, "duration": 3.881}, {"text": "This choice is particularly", "start": 902.639, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "significant because water is life. Water", "start": 906.079, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "is health, water is food security, water", "start": 908.48, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "is energy, and water is also in certain", "start": 911.44, "duration": 7.6}, {"text": "regions a matter of peace and stability.", "start": 915.6, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "We therefore call for", "start": 919.04, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "stronger international mobilization in", "start": 922.24, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "favor of universal access to safe", "start": 924.56, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "drinking water and sanitation,", "start": 926.56, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "particularly in rural areas", "start": 928.16, "duration": 8.039}, {"text": "and in the most vulnerable communities.", "start": 931.199, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "We invite our partners to view water", "start": 936.48, "duration": 7.359}, {"text": "not merely as a natural resource but as", "start": 940.0, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "as strategic investments in peace,", "start": 943.839, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "health and sustainable development.", "start": 946.399, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "Excellencies,", "start": 948.56, "duration": 3.519}, {"text": "with regard to socioeconomic", "start": 950.639, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "development, achieving the sustainable", "start": 952.079, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "development goals and those of agenda", "start": 955.12, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "2063", "start": 957.92, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "requires financial means that are", "start": 959.92, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "commeasurate with our ambitions. Yet,", "start": 962.72, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "many developing countries", "start": 965.6, "duration": 7.599}, {"text": "face considerable budgetary constraints,", "start": 968.56, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "high financing costs,", "start": 973.199, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "and a heavy debt burden.", "start": 975.68, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "We therefore call for a reform of the", "start": 978.16, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "international financial architecture", "start": 980.48, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "to make it more equitable, more", "start": 983.44, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "inclusive and better adapted to the", "start": 985.839, "duration": 6.481}, {"text": "realities of developing countries.", "start": 988.48, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "Such a reform must in particular provide", "start": 992.32, "duration": 6.639}, {"text": "access to predictable, affordable,", "start": 995.68, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "sustainable financing which is essential", "start": 998.959, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "for accelerating the implementation of", "start": 1001.92, "duration": 7.4}, {"text": "the SDGs and agenda 2063.", "start": 1003.839, "duration": 5.481}, {"text": "We must also", "start": 1010.16, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "empower Africa to play a more active", "start": 1013.36, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "role.", "start": 1015.279, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "Africa with its 55 states of more than 1", "start": 1017.759, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "billion400 million inhabitants cannot", "start": 1021.04, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "remain on the margins of the bodies that", "start": 1023.6, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "shape the rules of global trade. On", "start": 1026.079, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "behalf of the African Union, I reiterate", "start": 1028.64, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "our continent's call", "start": 1031.12, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "for", "start": 1034.64, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "full and equitable representation", "start": 1036.88, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "within the World Trade Organization.", "start": 1039.919, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "This is not a favor we are seeking. It", "start": 1043.76, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "is a demand for justice. It is also a", "start": 1046.319, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "guarantee of progress for the", "start": 1048.88, "duration": 6.799}, {"text": "entire multilateral trading system.", "start": 1051.84, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "With the African continental free trade", "start": 1055.679, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "area, our continent has already", "start": 1057.6, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "demonstrated its capacity", "start": 1059.84, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "to develop rules and to integrate", "start": 1062.24, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "markets.", "start": 1065.039, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "It is now up to global trade governance", "start": 1067.039, "duration": 7.921}, {"text": "to draw on this.", "start": 1071.12, "duration": 8.96}, {"text": "But in order to succeed, we must be more", "start": 1074.96, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "resilient in order to preserve an", "start": 1080.08, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "environment favorable to agriculture,", "start": 1082.0, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "a source of life and food security.", "start": 1085.12, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Indeed, Mr. President,", "start": 1087.28, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "climate change strikes the most", "start": 1089.76, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "vulnerable populations particularly", "start": 1093.039, "duration": 3.441}, {"text": "hard.", "start": 1095.039, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "Africa has contributed little to", "start": 1096.48, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "historical greenhouse gas emissions, yet", "start": 1099.6, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "it is already suffering severe", "start": 1102.799, "duration": 7.041}, {"text": "consequences. We therefore call for", "start": 1104.96, "duration": 7.76}, {"text": "stronger international solidarity", "start": 1109.84, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "on adaptation, climate financing, and", "start": 1112.72, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "technology transfer.", "start": 1115.6, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Food security must become", "start": 1117.679, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "a strategic priority", "start": 1120.24, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "because no sustainable development is", "start": 1123.039, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "possible when millions of families lack", "start": 1125.039, "duration": 6.721}, {"text": "sufficient and nutrition food nutritious", "start": 1128.96, "duration": 6.719}, {"text": "food. In closing,", "start": 1131.76, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "I would like to raise the question of", "start": 1135.679, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "youth, the most precious asset on which", "start": 1137.84, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "the entire international community can", "start": 1141.36, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "and must rely. I speak today", "start": 1143.44, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "Not only", "start": 1147.44, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "as a committed friend of young people", "start": 1149.919, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "but also on the basis of a clear", "start": 1152.88, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "observation. Our intellectual youth has", "start": 1154.799, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "become the target of sustained", "start": 1157.76, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "deliberate and organized pursuit by", "start": 1160.48, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "most of the wealthiest nations. Even", "start": 1164.24, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "though our youth's first calling should", "start": 1166.64, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "be to serve their parents, their loved", "start": 1169.12, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "ones, and their homeland who have", "start": 1171.6, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "invested so much in their education,", "start": 1174.64, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "many African states devote considerable", "start": 1178.48, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "resources to education,", "start": 1180.88, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "vocational training,", "start": 1183.76, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "entrepreneurship,", "start": 1185.919, "duration": 3.601}, {"text": "science,", "start": 1187.679, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "digital technology, and innovation.", "start": 1189.52, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "Yet, while our African nations such as", "start": 1192.88, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "Burundi", "start": 1195.6, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "make these major sacrifices to build", "start": 1197.2, "duration": 7.359}, {"text": "their future, these young talents are", "start": 1200.08, "duration": 7.839}, {"text": "prematurely lured away by actors who", "start": 1204.559, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "offer better material and financial", "start": 1207.919, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "conditions", "start": 1210.0, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "without", "start": 1211.76, "duration": 3.039}, {"text": "having needed to make any prior", "start": 1213.28, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "investment in their training.", "start": 1214.799, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "Let us be clear. It is imperative to", "start": 1217.44, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "establish a fair partnership so that our", "start": 1220.08, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "countries receive a fair return on the", "start": 1223.36, "duration": 6.559}, {"text": "investments made in the education of our", "start": 1227.36, "duration": 5.559}, {"text": "youth.", "start": 1229.919, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "The other actions we must all take also", "start": 1238.799, "duration": 7.521}, {"text": "include giving young people a real voice", "start": 1241.52, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "in decision-m peace and development", "start": 1246.32, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "processes.", "start": 1248.96, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Youth should not be regarded solely as", "start": 1252.0, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "beneficiaries of public policy.", "start": 1254.32, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "They must be integrated both upstream", "start": 1257.28, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "and downstream in the design and", "start": 1260.08, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "implementation of these policies.", "start": 1263.6, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "This is what would make it possible to", "start": 1266.32, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "create a secure future and restore hope", "start": 1270.0, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "to these young people.", "start": 1273.28, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "This emerged from the discussions at the", "start": 1276.0, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "fifth continental dialogue on youth", "start": 1279.039, "duration": 7.921}, {"text": "peace and security held in Bjin Bura", "start": 1281.919, "duration": 8.24}, {"text": "from August 10th to 12th, 2026. A", "start": 1286.96, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "dialogue that highlighted the link", "start": 1290.159, "duration": 3.281}, {"text": "between", "start": 1291.76, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "water, peace, conflict prevention,", "start": 1293.44, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "and inclusive leadership by young people", "start": 1297.76, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "and women.", "start": 1300.48, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "The discussions at this dialogue made it", "start": 1303.2, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "clear that there can be no lasting peace", "start": 1305.2, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "in Africa without the full effective and", "start": 1307.76, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "institutionalized participation of its", "start": 1311.36, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "youth. For too long, we have spoken of", "start": 1313.28, "duration": 7.92}, {"text": "youth as a generation called upon to", "start": 1318.08, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "take the reigns tomorrow. But African", "start": 1321.2, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "youth is not only the future of our", "start": 1323.52, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "continent,", "start": 1326.32, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "it must also be its present.", "start": 1328.159, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "We therefore call for strengthening the", "start": 1330.88, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "continental youth peace and security", "start": 1333.2, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "agenda and providing it with resources", "start": 1335.2, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "commenurate with its ambitions. We have", "start": 1338.64, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "a duty to create more opportunities for", "start": 1341.36, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "young people to contribute to conflict", "start": 1344.799, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "prevention, mediation, reconciliation,", "start": 1347.679, "duration": 7.401}, {"text": "and peace building.", "start": 1351.44, "duration": 3.64}, {"text": "As the current chairperson of the", "start": 1355.36, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "African Union and the champion of the", "start": 1357.12, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "youth peace and security agenda, I", "start": 1359.28, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "intend to continue championing this", "start": 1361.6, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "ambition. Finally, excellencies, ladies", "start": 1363.52, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "and gentlemen,", "start": 1366.24, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "turning to Burundi, we are pleased to", "start": 1368.64, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "continue its economic and social", "start": 1371.6, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "transformation within the framework of", "start": 1374.0, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "its vision Burundi 204060.", "start": 1376.24, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "We are determined to transform our", "start": 1380.24, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "agriculture,", "start": 1382.48, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "develop our infrastructure,", "start": 1384.32, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "improve access to energy and water,", "start": 1386.48, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "strengthen education and health, and", "start": 1390.24, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "promote a dynamic private sector.", "start": 1392.96, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "Our ambition is for Burundi to be an", "start": 1396.559, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "emerging country by 2040 and a developed", "start": 1398.88, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "country by60.", "start": 1401.28, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "We invite our partners to support this", "start": 1404.32, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "transformation", "start": 1406.72, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "not only through multifaceted assistance", "start": 1408.32, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "but also through investment", "start": 1411.36, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "technology transfer capacity building", "start": 1414.799, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "and the development of mutually", "start": 1418.64, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "beneficial partnerships.", "start": 1420.48, "duration": 7.199}, {"text": "Vision 2040 2060 has now become a", "start": 1423.919, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "central framework for national", "start": 1427.679, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "development planning.", "start": 1429.2, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "The African Union and the United Nations", "start": 1431.52, "duration": 7.039}, {"text": "share a particular responsibility", "start": 1435.52, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "in building a more peaceful and more", "start": 1438.559, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "just world.", "start": 1440.799, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "We must strengthen our partnership in", "start": 1443.679, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "the areas of peace and security,", "start": 1445.679, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "sustainable development,", "start": 1448.88, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "health, climate, youth, and global", "start": 1451.44, "duration": 6.52}, {"text": "governance.", "start": 1454.96, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "The AU UN partnership must be founded on", "start": 1458.72, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "mutual respect, complimentarity,", "start": 1462.24, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "and greater African ownership of", "start": 1466.0, "duration": 6.679}, {"text": "solutions to the continent's challenges.", "start": 1467.919, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "Africa wants to be a strategic partner", "start": 1472.72, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "and a full-fledged actor in", "start": 1475.12, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "multilateralism,", "start": 1477.12, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "not merely an area of intervention for", "start": 1479.12, "duration": 7.439}, {"text": "the international community.", "start": 1483.279, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "As Burundi assumes the chairmanship of", "start": 1486.559, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "the African Union, it is choosing unity,", "start": 1488.559, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "solidarity, and action. We are choosing", "start": 1490.96, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "an Africa at peace, an Africa that is", "start": 1494.32, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "integrated, an Africa that feeds itself,", "start": 1497.279, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "and an Africa that transforms its", "start": 1500.0, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "resources,", "start": 1502.4, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "an Africa that empowers its youth to", "start": 1504.08, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "create and innovate, an Africa that is", "start": 1506.88, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "master of its own destiny. And we are", "start": 1509.919, "duration": 6.961}, {"text": "choosing a renewed multilateralism", "start": 1512.88, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "in which every region,", "start": 1516.88, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "every people and every nation counts", "start": 1519.36, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "for Africa. We want a United Nations", "start": 1522.32, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "that is more representative, more", "start": 1526.0, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "effective, and closer to the peoples. We", "start": 1528.64, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "want an Africa that is better", "start": 1532.08, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "represented within global", "start": 1535.039, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "decision-making bodies.", "start": 1537.679, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "We want a global partnership founded not", "start": 1540.559, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "on dependency but on solidarity, shared", "start": 1543.84, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "responsibility", "start": 1547.2, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "and investment in the future. On behalf", "start": 1549.2, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "of the people of Burundi", "start": 1552.88, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "and in our capacity as the chairperson", "start": 1555.76, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "of the African Union, we call on all our", "start": 1558.159, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "partners.", "start": 1562.4, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "Let us make this period of", "start": 1564.48, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "transformation an opportunity to build a", "start": 1566.0, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "more just world, a stronger Africa, and", "start": 1569.2, "duration": 8.079}, {"text": "a better future for generations to come.", "start": 1573.44, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "Bernundi and the African Union express", "start": 1577.279, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "the hope that the high level debate of", "start": 1579.679, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "this 81st session", "start": 1582.32, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "of the United Nations General Assembly", "start": 1585.039, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "will mark a new beginning for a", "start": 1588.159, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "consolidated multilateralism.", "start": 1591.2, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "A United Nations in which every state", "start": 1593.84, "duration": 7.959}, {"text": "and every region counts. Thank you.", "start": 1596.799, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "On behalf of the general assembly, I", "start": 1609.12, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "wish to thank the president of the", "start": 1612.72, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "republic of Bundi.", "start": 1614.799, "duration": 3.641}]